{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"effusive-unsentient-massasauga","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\n`tests/scripts/test_run_reconcile_bridge_heldout.py:224-232` (`test_legacy_engine_dispositions_remain_visible_to_direct_callers`) still does `sys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT / \"src\" / \"rebar\" / \"_engine\"))` before `from rebar.reconciler.guarded_pass import _Disposition`, then pops it in `finally`. That is the old by-path engine loader shape. Since S1 (gunshy-symmetric-barnacle) the reconciler is the ordinary package `rebar.reconciler`. `src/rebar/_engine` holds no Python package: `git ls-tree` lists only `jira-capability-probe.py` and `resources/`. So the insert loads nothing, and the import resolves through the installed package anyway. It is the only remaining `sys.path.insert` under `tests/` that exists to make `rebar.reconciler` resolvable, and it keeps epic friended-brainsick-degus criterion 1 from holding. Cites are on origin/main 5bc443bdd96.\n\n## Approach\n1. In that test, replace the `sys.path.insert` / `try` / `finally: sys.path.pop(0)` block with a plain `from rebar.reconciler.guarded_pass import _Disposition` at the top of the test body. Keep all 5 assertions unchanged.\n2. Drop the `sys` and `ROOT` imports from the module if nothing else in it uses them. `ROOT` is imported from `test_run_reconcile_bridge`, and `sys` is still used by `test_shallow_checkout_is_rejected_before_reconciliation` (`sys.executable`), so `sys` stays. Ruff decides what is unused.\n3. Out of scope: the `_engine` path inserts in `tests/scripts/conftest.py:28`, `tests/scripts/reducer/*` and `tests/scripts/graph/test_graph_cycles.py:275`. They target the reducer and graph packages, not the reconciler.\n\n## Scope\n`tests/scripts/test_run_reconcile_bridge_heldout.py` only. No source, docs, or baseline change.\n\n## Testing\n`pytest tests/scripts/test_run_reconcile_bridge_heldout.py -q`; `ruff check tests/scripts/test_run_reconcile_bridge_heldout.py`; `make verify`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `git grep -nE 'sys\\.path\\.insert' -- tests/scripts/test_run_reconcile_bridge_heldout.py` prints nothing.\n- [ ] `test_legacy_engine_dispositions_remain_visible_to_direct_callers` passes with its 5 assertions unchanged.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] `make verify` exits 0.\n  provenance: environment=local dev host; principal=Rebar Bot Nava; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — run log on the ticket","id":"4b07-4291-8d1e-48b2","parent_id":"ebf5-5d21-0124-4313","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Drop the last _engine sys.path insert for the reconciler from the bridge heldout test"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1792673331462858357,"uuid":"60082409-3106-42df-b7ab-e26b0d5a6332"}